  "plan": "Explore the environment: check for gcc/g++, python3, numpy, zlib, libpng headers, and internet access to MNIST. This determines my approach for training the model and decoding the PNG. Based on results I'll either use libpng or write a manual PNG decoder (using zlib for inflate).",
  "commands": [
    {"keystrokes": "cd /app && ls -la\n", "duration": 0.2},
    {"keystrokes": "which gcc g++ python3 curl; echo '---'; python3 --version\n", "duration": 0.3},
    {"keystrokes": "python3 -c \"import numpy; print('numpy', numpy.__version__)\" 2>&1\n", "duration": 0.5},
    {"keystrokes": "ls /usr/include/png.h /usr/include/zlib.h 2>&1; echo '---'; ldconfig -p 2>/dev/null | grep -Ei 'png|z'\n", "duration": 0.3},
    {"keystrokes": "timeout 6 curl -sI http://yann.lecun.com/exdb/mnist/train-images-idx3-ubyte.gz 2>&1 | head -5; echo DONE\n", "duration": 7.0}
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "Key findings: /app already contains useful scaffolding: cJSON (JSON in C), lodepng (self-contained PNG decoder in C++), a test image.png, model.pth (PyTorch, 54KB), and model.py. However, there is NO gcc/g++/clang, NO curl, NO numpy, and NO torch. libz.so.1 exists at runtime. I need to: (1) understand model.py architecture, (2) find a compiler to build the C++ cli_tool, (3) figure out how to load model.pth without torch. Let me investigate further.",
  "plan": "1) Read model.py to learn the architecture. 2) Search for any C/C++ compiler (cc, clang, tcc, gcc). 3) Check if torch/pip are available. 4) Inspect model.pth structure. This determines my strategy for producing weights.json and the binary.",
  "commands": [
    {"keystrokes": "cat model.py\n", "duration": 0.2},
    {"keystrokes": "ls /usr/bin | grep -iE 'gcc|clang|cc|tcc|g\\+\\+|ld|as|cc1' ; echo '==='; which cc clang gcc g++ tcc 2>&1\n", "duration": 0.3},
    {"keystrokes": "python3 -c \"import torch; print('torch', torch.__version__)\" 2>&1 | head -3\n", "duration": 1.0},
    {"keystrokes": "python3 -m pip --version 2>&1; which pip pip3 2>&1\n", "duration": 0.5},
    {"keystrokes": "file model.pth; python3 -c \"import zipfile,sys; z=zipfile.ZipFile('model.pth'); print(z.namelist()[:20])\" 2>&1 | head -30\n", "duration": 1.0}
  ]
}

