  "analysis": "model.py defines a 2-hidden-layer MLP: input_layer Linear(input_dim, hidden_dim), hidden_layer Linear(hidden_dim, hidden_dim), output_layer Linear(hidden_dim, 10), with ReLU between. The /usr/bin listing shows NO C/C++ compiler (gcc/clang/cc/tcc) and no curl. The last two commands (pip version, model.pth zip listing) got merged and didn't show output. I need to determine: (a) is torch/numpy/pip available, (b) is there ANY compiler anywhere on the system, (c) the internal structure of model.pth so I can extract weights. This dictates whether cli_tool must be a Python script (no compiler) or a compiled C++ binary (using lodepng + cJSON).",
